\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For finite X and any $r\in F(X)$, is $\langle X|r\rangle $ word-hyperbolic whenever it contains no subgroup isomorphic to BS(m,n) for any nonzero integers m,n?

\subsection{Short English statement}
For finite X and any $r\in F(X)$, is $\langle X|r\rangle $ word-hyperbolic whenever it contains no subgroup isomorphic to BS(m,n) for any nonzero integers m,n?

