\section*{Hyperbolicity of one-relator groups without Baumslag–Solitar subgroups}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents a proof in the selected manuscript. A finitely generated one-relator group without any nontrivial-parameter Baumslag--Solitar subgroup is claimed hyperbolic.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Intersection and commensurator bounds reduce the problem to a restricted HNN setting. Annular diagrams generate a stationary current with finite carriers; failure of expansion would give periodic line trajectories and a forbidden Baumslag--Solitar configuration, completing the hyperbolicity argument.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
The group has a finite generating set and one defining relator. Excluding all Baumslag--Solitar subgroups with both integer parameters nonzero is claimed enough for hyperbolicity, exactly the implication in this question. This is presented as a claimed affirmative answer.

